WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.567
-Good evening, everybody.
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:04.067
This is "Late Night."
How's everybody doing tonight?

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:05.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
Good to hear.

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:08.934
In that case,
let's get to the news.

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:12.968
After President Biden met last
week with the K-pop band BTS,

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:16.133
the White House posted a video
to Instagram that showed

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:18.501
Biden playing the group's
hit song, "Butter."

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:21.000
But they cut out the part
where he asked them to please

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.868
write a song about something
he's allowed to have.

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:26.868
"Smooth like hummus.
How about that?"

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:28.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:30.834
President Biden delivered
an address on Thursday night

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:33.300
from the White House
and called on Congress

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.667
to pass gun-safety legislation,
which is kind of like

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:40.133
calling on the Jets
to win the Super Bowl.

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:42.267
You can ask.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:43.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.834 --> 00:00:46.300
That's right. President Biden
delivered an address

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.434
on Thursday night
and called on Congress to ban

00:00:48.434 --> 00:00:51.534
assault-style weapons
and expand background checks.

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:54.767
Or at the very least,
get rid of the vending machines.

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:56.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.934 --> 00:01:00.133
Dr. Mehmet Oz last week won
Pennsylvania's Republican

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:02.133
Senate primary,
which seems a little crazy.

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:05.901
I mean, is he even qualified
to be a doctor?

00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:08.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.934
The House select committee
investigating the Capitol attack

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:13.467
will hold its first public
hearing on Thursday,

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:16.501
so we can all finally get to
the bottom of that thing

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:19.634
the entire country watched on
live TV in real time.

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:24.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:29.167
A man recently threw cake
on the protective glass of

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:31.100
Leonardo da Vinci's
"Mona Lisa" painting

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.501
at the Louvre in Paris.

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:35.968
He also threw some on a Picasso,
but no one noticed.

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:37.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:41.534
Yeah, we'll go after Picasso.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.934
You're not off the hook,
Picasso.

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:45.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:48.467
Yesterday was National Hot Air
Balloon Day.

00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:51.400
This news was first reported by
a very apologetic

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.033
JetBlue gate agent.

00:01:53.033 --> 00:02:01.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.567
Baze and I talked backstage,

00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:05.901
and we were like, "I think we
put JetBlue on the balloon."

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:08.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:10.667
You know what? I don't think it
would have mattered either way.

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:12.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:14.901
During a para--

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.701
So, did you guys even
understand, though?

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:18.133
I feel like you guys
don't even under--

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:19.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:21.501
You buy a ticket
on a JetBlue flight

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:23.400
and then you get to the gate
and they have to apologize

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.367
and be like, "We're very sorry,
it's Hot Air Balloon Day.

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:26.701
You got to ride
a hot air balloon."

00:02:26.701 --> 00:02:31.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:33.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:34.834
You know --

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:36.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:39.367
We were on hiatus.
We're all a little rusty.

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:40.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:44.601
During a parade over the weekend
honoring her platinum jubilee,

00:02:44.601 --> 00:02:46.334
a hologram of Queen Elizabeth

00:02:46.334 --> 00:02:48.200
was shown in
her gold stagecoach.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.834
And whatever you think
of the Queen,

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:52.000
her duet with Tupac was amazing.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:59.067
And finally, New York's
LaGuardia Airport

00:02:59.067 --> 00:03:02.534
over the weekend debuted its
newly-renovated Terminal C,

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:05.601
which features an 11-lane
security screening area.

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:08.267
And this is cool --
one of them is open!

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:09.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:12.300
And that was the monologue,
everybody.

